What was changed in references/board-critique.md, by Record Evolution GmbH
in 2026:

- The text is new wording throughout, written as checks that an agent runs
  on an IronFlock board it built or restyled, before it reports it.
- Kept and condensed: the five dimensions of the critique (first
  impression, usability, visual hierarchy, consistency, accessibility) and
  the questions behind them.
- Changed: each check names what to look at in a board's definition (its
  pages, widget types, tile sizes and positions, titles, style, state
  colours and bindings), so that it can be answered without an image, and
  what to correct; the checks are run once, with one round of corrections.
- Left out: the request for a design file or a screenshot, the feedback
  style and the report format, typography and whitespace, the connectors
  to design tools and user feedback, and the tips.

What was changed in references/board-charts.md, by Record Evolution GmbH in
2026:

- The text is new wording throughout, written as rules for the widgets of
  IronFlock boards, each naming the widget setting that applies it.
- Kept and condensed: the chart chosen by what the data shows, and when a
  number or a table serves better; categories sorted by value unless they
  have an order of their own; bars from zero, lines allowed to leave it;
  the same scale on charts that are compared; few categories and series;
  titles and labelled axes with units; values written on the bars; colour
  that encodes data; never colour alone; colours that hold for red-green
  colour-blind readers.
- Changed: the title says what is measured, not the finding, because a
  board's data is live; the palette is per board preset and keeps clear of
  the state colours.
- Added: the order in which the board hands rows to a widget, fixed time
  buckets for amounts per period, the same period on compared charts,
  splitting a chart per entity, the colours a theme gives a series left
  without one, recolouring on a restyle, doughnut slices and the state
  column of tables.
- Left out: the Python plotting code, chart types IronFlock has no widget
  for, 3D charts, pattern fills and point markers, highlighting one series
  against grey, annotations, error bars, alt text, number formatting,
  typography and the checklist: no widget setting applies them.

What was changed in references/board-interaction.md, by Record Evolution
GmbH in 2026:

- The text is new wording throughout, written as rules that each name the
  setting of an IronFlock board widget that applies them.
- Kept and condensed: buttons labelled by what their click does; the same
  word for the same thing everywhere; errors that say what happened and
  what to do; empty states that say why and how to start; confirmations
  that name the action and its consequence, with buttons named by the
  action; contrast thresholds for text and for other parts; touch target
  sizes (accessibility-review); an action keeping its name through the
  flow and errors that neither apologise nor stay vague (the part on
  writing of frontend-design).
- Added: touch target sizes in pixels and fixed grid cells, derived from
  the physical size of a pixel; the alarm red for the Delete button per
  look; the widget settings for each rule.
- Left out: keyboard, focus and screen-reader checks, the audit and copy
  report formats, tone tables, tooltips, loading and onboarding copy, the
  connectors, and everything of frontend-design outside its part on
  writing.

